OL,3,GNEWSABrothers who both had meningitis
OL,4,Awithin a year lucky to be alive
OL,5,
OL,6,FTwo brothers who contracted meningitis
OL,7,Fwithin a year of each other say they
OL,8,Fare lucky to be alive.
OL,10,FSaul and Drew Darlington from Wrexham,
OL,11,Fnow 29 and 26, initially thought it was
OL,12,Fa "weird" coincidence they both caught
OL,13,Fthe illness as teenagers but later
OL,14,Flearnt they had a rare condition which
OL,15,Fmeant they were susceptible to it.
OL,17,F"The day I had it, if I had gone to
OL,18,Fsleep that night, I'd have probably
OL,19,Fdied," said Saul who, along with his
OL,20,Fbrother, now wants to raise awareness
OL,21,Fof the symptoms of meningitis,
OL,22,Fparticularly among young people.
OL,23,APub: 28-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBWales NewsC Reg TVFClean Feed
